$$-4x + ky = 5$$', NULL, $lyceon_json$[{"key":"A","text":"$-6$"},{"key":"B","text":"$6$"},{"key":"C","text":"$9$"},{"key":"D","text":"$-9$"}]$lyceon_json$::jsonb, 'B', NULL, E'A system has no solution when the lines are parallel but not coincident, meaning the ratios of corresponding coefficients are equal but the ratio of constants differs. Setting the coefficient ratios equal: $\\frac{6}{-4} = \\frac{-9}{k}$. Cross-multiplying gives $6k = (-4)(-9) = 36$, so $k = 6$. With $k = 6$, the constant ratio is $\\frac{14}{5}$, which differs from the coefficient ratio $-\\frac{3}{2}$, confirming the lines are parallel and non-coincident. The value $-6$ comes from incorrectly applying a negative sign when cross-multiplying. The value 9 results from copying the coefficient from the first equation without computing the required proportionality. The value $-9$ arises from assuming the $y$-coefficients must be negatives of each other rather than checking the full proportionality condition.', $lyceon_json${"A":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"sign_error"},"B":{"role":"correct","error_taxonomy":null},"C":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"partial_reasoning"},"D":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"concept_gap"}}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, NULL, 'draft', 1, 105, false, $lyceon_json${"provenance":"Lyceon original","authored_by":"claude","authored_date":"2026-08-27"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, $lyceon_json${"model":"claude","generation_date":"2026-08-27","prompt_version":"questions_governance_v1"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb);
































